World "Lagrange"
Title "Lagrange's Theorem"

Introduction "
Each coset of a finite subgroup has the same size as the subgroup.
Since the cosets partition the group, we can count the group by counting its cosets.
This gives Lagrange's theorem: the size of a subgroup divides the size of the group.
"
